_hit.html

# Raw capture GIFs. gen/walkthroughs.py turns them into the mp4s that ship;
# committing both pays twice for the same frames.
assets/video/_gif/

# One-shot scripts at the ROOT only. Anchored, because an unanchored _*.py also
# swallowed gen/__init__.py and content/__init__.py, without which `python -m gen.x`
# does not work at all on a fresh clone.
/_*.py

# The fonts ARE in the repo now, and that is the point of them.
#
# This folder used to hold 11 commercial faces (PP Kyoto, ABC Diatype, Apercu Mono,
# P22 Mackinac, Monument Grotesk), ignored wholesale because committing them to a
# public repository is redistribution and git history makes that permanent. The site
# then fell through to a Google Fonts @import, which meant the published page never
# looked like the design at all.
#
# gen/fonts.py replaced all of it with four families cut from open-licensed sources
# and named for this site. Those .woff2 files and the OFL-*.txt beside them are
# tracked, because a font the reader cannot download is not serving anybody.
#
# What stays out: the variable-font masters the cuts come from, which are 2MB to
# ship 180KB and are re-fetched by the generator on demand, and any .otf or .ttf,
# which is either a licensed original that must not be published or an intermediate
# nobody needs.
assets/fonts/_src/
assets/fonts/*.otf
assets/fonts/*.ttf
